wasix-libc (2025.12.24.1+ds-2) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * d/patches: Fix FTBFS with clang 23 (Closes: #1154036)
    - Pass --target=wasm32-wasip1 to the compiler, as --target=wasm32-wasi
      is deprecated since clang 22 and fatal with -Werror. The installation
      paths keep using wasm32-wasi.
    - Filter out the predefined macros new to clang 23 in check-symbols,
      so that the expected metadata matches with both clang 21 and 23.
  * d/rules: Pass CC, AR and NM on the make command line, so that the
    package is always built with clang/llvm even if CC=gcc comes from the
    environment or MAKEFLAGS.
  * d/patches: Drop 0001-Fix-build-errors.patch. It pointed the
    libwasi-emulated-getpid sources at libc-bottom-half/sources/getpid,
    which does not exist (getpid() is implemented in sources/getpid.c and
    is part of libc.a), so it had no effect on the built package.
  * d/copyright: Drop libclang_rt.builtins-wasm32.a from Files-Excluded.
    It was removed upstream in 2025.07.01.1, and the stale entry makes
    uscan/mk-origtargz warn that no files matched the excluded pattern.
  * d/watch: Convert to format version 5 (older-debian-watch-file-standard).
  * d/control: Bump Standards-Version to 4.7.4 (no changes needed).
  * d/control: Drop redundant Priority: optional and Rules-Requires-Root: no
    fields from the source stanza.
  * Bump debhelper compat level to 14.
    - d/control: Drop Depends, as dh_gencontrol now adds ${misc:Depends}
      and ${shlibs:Depends} automatically. This also fixes the
      "${shlibs:Depends} used, but is not defined" warning.
    - d/rules: Run dh --without single-binary, as files are installed to
      debian/tmp through the upstream INSTALL_DIR variable.
  * d/copyright: Exclude the empty git submodule directories
    tools/llvm-project and tools/{wasi,wasix}-headers/WASI, which made
    dpkg-source warn about ignoring their deletion.
  * d/rules: Copy the built sysroot in override_dh_auto_install instead of
    running "make install", which compiled the whole library a second time.

 -- Fukui Daichi <a.dog.will.talk@akane.waseda.jp>  Sun, 22 Nov 2026 16:00:00 +0000

